Requirements:
In addition to the general requirements of the university for admission as a classified graduate student, the Department of Justice Studies requires that a student:

1. have a baccalaureate degree with a major in Criminology, Administration of Justice, or a related field (e.g., one of the social sciences, such as sociology, political science, psychology, etc.);
2. have a grade point average of 3.0 or better (on a 4.0 scale) in the last 60 semester/90 quarter units;
3. achieve a satisfactory score on the Graduate Record Exam (GRE) (verbal, quantitative, and analytical sections);
4. submit two letters of recommendation;
5. submit a one-page statement of purpose; and
6. submit a writing sample (a five-page, double-spaced essay).
